---

Write feature PRD for {{.id}}: "{{.title}}".

CHECK COMPLEXITY TIER: Read feature metadata via {{template "get_json" .}} | jq -r '.metadata.complexity_tier' (values: SIMPLE, STANDARD, COMPLEX).

LOAD: specification-writing workflow write-feature-prd.md.

READ:
(1) Triage report or research report for file estimates and integration points
(2) Parent epic PRD for scope boundaries and requirements traceability
(3) Feature description at {{.file_path}}
(4) Other feature PRDs in this epic for consistency

SCALE OUTPUT BY TIER:
- SIMPLE (should not normally reach BA, but if so: 1-page summary with goal, key user story, core acceptance criteria only)
- STANDARD (focused PRD: goal, key personas, MoSCoW user stories, core functional requirements, testable acceptance criteria, out of scope -- 2-3 pages max, omit less critical sections)
- COMPLEX (full 6-file PRD per write-feature-prd.md: epic.md style goal, personas.md, user-journeys.md, requirements.md, success-metrics.md, scope.md)

Requirements must trace to epic requirements.

EXIT GATE varies by tier:
- SIMPLE (core AC testable)
- STANDARD (MoSCoW complete, AC testable, no ambiguity)
- COMPLEX (all 6 files, write-feature-prd.md checklist passes)
